From abb2bcf202067a6667fd50ee8d4d3b68a99e97ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 08:30:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] SurfaceFlinger: Disable modeset_state_machine flag for GSI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The modeset_state_machine feature flag, added in AOSP QPR2, causes
two display issues on GSI installations with multi-rate displays
(e.g. 60Hz+120Hz):

1. Boot deadlock: The flag changes isModeSetPending() to check
   pendingModeOpt instead of the legacy isModeSetPending field. When
   SF requests 120Hz during init via applyActiveMode(), a pending
   mode is set that can only be cleared by finalizeDisplayModeChange.
   But commit() blocks on isFramePending+isModeSetPending before
   finalization can occur, and no frame can be presented to signal
   the fence. Result: permanent black screen.

2. Garbled boot graphics: When the first SF instance dies mid-mode-
   change (normal on GSI — SF restarts once during init), the flag's
   state machine leaves HWC in a partially-configured state. The
   second SF instance sees the mode as already active and skips
   reinitialization, inheriting the corrupted display state.

Disable by overriding FlagManager::modeset_state_machine() to return
false, restoring the pre-QPR2 modeset behavior.
---
 services/surfaceflinger/common/FlagManager.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/common/FlagManager.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/common/FlagManager.cpp
index 4bb4d5b..bc07806 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/common/FlagManager.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/common/FlagManager.cpp
@@ -285,7 +285,14 @@ FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(graphite_renderengine, "debug.renderengine.graphite")
 FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(hdcp_level_hal, "")
 FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(hdcp_negotiation, "debug.sf.hdcp_negotiation");
 FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(local_tonemap_screenshots, "debug.sf.local_tonemap_screenshots");
-FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(modeset_state_machine, "");
+// [GSI] Disable modeset_state_machine to prevent display deadlock and corruption
+// on devices with multi-rate displays (e.g. 60Hz+120Hz). This AOSP QPR2 feature
+// flag creates a chicken-and-egg deadlock during boot: the mode change can't
+// finalize until a frame is presented, but commit() blocks frame presentation
+// until the mode change finalizes. It also causes garbled graphics when SF dies
+// mid-mode-change and the second SF instance inherits stale HWC state.
+// Other QPR2 GSI builds that predate this flag do not have these issues.
+bool FlagManager::modeset_state_machine() const { return false; }
 FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(no_vsyncs_on_screen_off, "debug.sf.no_vsyncs_on_screen_off")
 FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(pacesetter_selection, "debug.sf.pacesetter_selection")
 FLAG_MANAGER_ACONFIG_FLAG(parse_edid_version_and_input_type,
